        "id": "RG-IDENTITY",
        "observation": "Mutable ordinary records and arrays receive cached public projections from their first read. The graph retains public aliases/cycles and explicit read/result refresh identity. Frozen inert graphs remain raw, and mutable descendants or accessors force their frozen parents to project.",
        "authority": [
          "M-EXPOSE-0001-G/H",
          "C-EXPOSE-0006-C/D/E",
          "C-EXPOSE-0008-B/C/D",
          "C-CONTEXT-0003-A"
        ],
        "compatibility": "The two changed mutable-data raw===public assertions were stronger than the catalog. Public-to-raw equality and write-through of ordinary mutable data are not preserved. This is an explicit compatibility change, not a general claim that all mutable-value changes are harmless."
      },
      {
        "id": "RG-SNAPSHOT",
        "observation": "This remains an explicit snapshot model. Each own accessor is sampled once at read/result; projected members remain writable data properties. Author raw mutation appears at the next explicit boundary; direct writes to a mutable public projection change that projection rather than its author source and are overwritten on a later raw refresh. Method receivers remain the author objects. Opaque values and immutable raw nodes retain their previous treatment.",
        "limits": "This is not a general live object membrane. It does not promise automatic observation/wrapping of arbitrary consumer mutations or descriptor fidelity."
      },
      {
        "id": "RG-KEYS",
        "observation": "Reflect.ownKeys preserves nested symbol/nonenumerable members and enumerability. Array length has separate handling. Registry filtering is identity-scoped and propagates to cached root projections and detached root copies, including old registries returned after replacement. Mutable nominal StyleHandle is not universally frozen; raw-identity retention is limited to truly frozen inert graphs, not all presentation-shaped values."
      },
      {
        "id": "RG-CANCEL-COMPOSITION",
        "observation": "The graph funnels callable entries through the same wrapCallable function. The trusted-cancellation predicate runs before ordinary callable caches, leaves only actual Module-issued trackedOff identities exempt, and does not expose registration. New registryRecords tracks object roles only; it cannot bless a lookalike callback. Function values are not cloned, so actual trackedOff WeakSet membership survives the new graph path.",
        "limits": "Static composition reasoning only; no combined runtime acceptance yet."
      }
    ],
